invariant: INV-14
file: srv_parser.c
catches: srv_quic_test
reason: the parser no longer refuses a second extension of one type, which RFC
  9846 §4.3 forbids (rfc9846.txt:1673-1674). The frozen digest depends on
  that refusal: it adds the extensions in ascending type order, and of two
  extensions with one type it adds only the first. So a second ClientHello
  that repeats an extension keeps the first hello's digest, and the retry
  check accepts a hello that added an extension. test/srv_quic_retry_tests.h
  sends ngtcp2's second hello with encrypt_then_mac twice and requires
  illegal_parameter.

--- old
    if (srv_ext_duplicate(exts, exts_len)) {
--- new
    if (0 && srv_ext_duplicate(exts, exts_len)) {
